# NestedText v3 - DTD-variants remainder transmigration, second of the deferred expansions (measured 2026-09-16)
# Source: D:\CLAUDE_CODE_COMMANDER\artifacts\_sweep\byproducts\$ARGUMENTS_VARIANT_EXAMPLES_DTD_VARIANTS.md sections 3.5-9.
# dtd-variants.nt holds the skeleton with duo/treis/tessares/pente parts;
# this file holds the NDATA, comparison, polyglot, injection and SGML
# mechanisms distilled. Ordinal: hex, next in the dtd-variants family.

ndata-deep-dive:
    > NDATA names the unparsed: an entity with a NOTATION, a path and no
    > content, the parser hands it to the application untouched. Generated
    > from $@ as asset lists (logo.png chart.svg data.csv): one entity per
    > file, the document references, never embeds. Binary beside XML is
    > NDATA with or without the NOTATION line; the krita DOC/IMAGE shape
    > is the same idea in a loose grammar.

comparison-matrix:
    > PCDATA escapes five chars (& < > " ') and normalizes whitespace
    > (newlines and tabs to spaces, runs to one); CDATA preserves exactly
    > and escapes nothing; NDATA carries no characters at all. The ]]>
    > collision terminates CDATA early: an arg containing ]]> must be
    > split, never trusted. Three contents, three contracts, chosen by
    > what the content is, never by convenience.

polyglot-layers:
    > Bash generates XML/DTD, YAML, NestedText, callouts, JSON and the
    > five-layer stack through CDATA extraction: XML holds CDATA, CDATA
    > holds NestedText, NestedText renders the callout. Each layer is a
    > pure function of the one below; a layer that re-parses is a layer
    > that can inject, so extraction flows one way only.

injection-vectors:
    > XXE via $@ (external entity reads files: disable DTD processing,
    > whitelist, CDATA for untrusted); CDATA termination (]]> split);
    > PCDATA escape bypass (attribute breakout: escape all five);
    > NDATA path traversal (validate the path, never resolve blind);
    > parameter-entity DTD injection (parameter entities never take user
    > input); Billion Laughs (recursive entities: cap expansion depth).
    > Six vectors, six fixes, each a trust rule the subsets state.

sgml-extensions:
    > SDATA (specific glyph data) and RCDATA (replaceable character data)
    > exist in SGML and not in XML: the corpus's DTDs are XML-subset, so
    > neither appears, and any SGML intake names them before parsing.

release-binding:
    > Stream 1 (trust): the six vectors are the XML half of the trust
    > evidence beside the shell five; untrusted content rides CDATA or
    > PCDATA-escaped, never raw, never eval. Stream 4 (forms): PCDATA vs
    > CDATA vs NDATA is the content contract behind every form choice.
